.TH LT-QWWAD_CHARGE_DENSITY "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_charge_density (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_charge_density \- generate a charge density profile for a 2D system.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_charge_density
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find charge density in a 2D heterostructure.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-wffileprefix\fR arg (=wf_e)
Prefix of wavefunction filenames.
.TP
\fB\-\-wffileext\fR arg (=.r)
File extension for wavefunction files.
.TP
\fB\-\-energyfile\fR arg (=Ee.r)
Filename of energy file.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-nper\fR ] arg (=1)
Number of periods crossed by the
wavefunction. This is only relevant for
periodic heterostructures.
.TP
\fB\-\-dopingfile\fR arg (=d.r)
File from which to read volume doping
profile [m^{\-3}]
.TP
\fB\-\-populationfile\fR arg (=N.r)
File from which to read subband
populations [m^{\-2}]
.TP
\fB\-\-degeneracyfile\fR arg
File from which to read subband
degeneracies. If not specified, all states
are taken to be non\-degenerate
.TP
\fB\-\-chargefile\fR arg (=cd.r)
File to which charge density profile will
be written
.TP
\fB\-\-carrierdensityfile\fR arg (=dens.r) File to which electron density profile
will be written
.TP
\fB\-\-ptype\fR
Dopants are to be treated as acceptors,
and wavefunctions treated as hole states
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'Ee.r'    Energy of each state:
             Column 1: state index.
             Column 2: energy [meV].

   'wf_ei.r' Wave function amplitude at each position:
             Column 1: position [m].
             Column 2: wave function amplitude [m^{-1/2}].

   'd.r'     Doping profile:
             Column 1: spatial location [m]
             Column 2: volume doping [m^{-3}]

   'N.r'     Subband populations:
             Column 1: population [m^{-2}]

.SS Output files:
   'cd.r'    Charge density profile:
             Column 1: spatial location [m]
             Column 2: volume density [C m^{-3}]

   'dens.r'  Carrier density profile:
             Column 1: spatial location [m]
             Column 2: volume density [m^{-3}]

Input data should be provided for ONE period of the doping
profile, and for all wavefunctions localised in that period.
If the wavefunctions have tails that extend over multiple periods
of a heterostructure, then use the --nper flag to specify how many.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute the charge density for a given (single-period) structure:
    qwwad_charge_density

Compute the charge density for a periodic structure, where the wf_e*.r files contain centrally-localised wavefunction data for three periods of the system.
    qwwad_charge_density --nper 3
.SH "CHARGE PROFILES"
The charge profile is generated by computing the distribution of carriers and subtracting their charge from the profile of donor ions.
The carrier distribution is obtained from the wavefunctions and populations of each subband.
By default, the carriers are assumed to be electrons, and the dopants to be positive donor ions.
To change this behaviour, use the --ptype flag.
